originate<br>&gt; from -- for example -- using &quot;0&quot; instead of &qu=
ot;&quot; in HKDF-Expand-Label?<br>&gt; I think depending on HMAC construct=
ion used, this might lead to<br>&gt; security concerns, generating unexpect=
ed keys and breaking the key<br>&gt; =C2=A0agreement at the very least.<br>=
<br>I&#39;m not a cryptographer but I don&#39;t know of any impacts.=C2=A0 =
Glancing<br>quickly at the specification, it doesn&#39;t appear that there =
are any<br>situations where you could have either &quot;&quot; or some valu=
e, so I don&#39;t<br>*think* there&#39;s room for ambiguity here. I&#39;m n=
ot sure what you mean by<br>&quot;depending on HMAC construction used&quot;=
, as HMAC is a single<br>construction just instantiated with hashes.=C2=A0 =
I agree it would be good<br>to get some confirmation here.<br><br><br>&gt; =
